Comments:
Evaluated by Caleb Marshall 2025
1) Observed resonances taken from Parker 1968, Couch 1971, Rolfs 1972a, Gorres 2000, and Becker 1982. All resonances normalized to 1258 keV resonance strength from Becker 1982.
2) Direct capture estimated from spectroscopic factors reported in Cooper 1986.
3) Resonance parameters for subthreshold and low lying resonances determined from recommended resonance strengths and lifetimes reported in Rolfs 1972b and Rolfs 1972c. The only
exception is the 883 keV resonance, where the alpha and gamma widths are nearly equal. In this case the Gg/G ratio reported in Gorodetzky 1966 was corrected using
the branching ratio reported in Rolfs and used to determine the partial widths.
4) For the 237 keV resonance upper limit, the upper limit on Ga was taken from the upper limit given by Couch 1971. Following the 2010 evaluation, since this state has T=1 there is a suppression factor of 1000 applied to the mean reduced width of the PT distribution. However, this time the uncertainty on this reduction factor is include in the sampling and given a factor of 10 uncertainty.